module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveBundle.AffineTwistSections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistPowers.Clause
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.NonvanishingPullback.Nonvanishing

/-!
# `D₊(s)` is where the degree-one section attached to `s` does not vanish

Let `A` be a commutative ring and `M` an `A`-module, so that `Proj(Sym_A M)` is the projective
bundle `𝐏(M̃)` over `Spec A`. An element `s : M` determines a global section
`SymmetricAlgebra.toTwistSections A M s` of `𝒪(1)` on `Proj(Sym_A M)`, namely the section
attached to `s` read as a degree-one element `ι A M s` of the symmetric algebra. This file
proves that the locus where that section does not vanish is exactly the standard open
`D₊(ι A M s)`, and then transports the statement along a morphism `f : Y ⟶ Proj(Sym_A M)`: the
inverse image `f⁻¹(D₊(ι A M s))` is the nonvanishing locus on `Y` of the pulled-back section
`f⁎s` of `f⁎𝒪(1)`. The pullback form is the local step of clause 3 of [Stacks, Tag 0B3V]: a
morphism whose pulled-back section generates `f⁎𝒪(1)` at every point factors through
`D₊(ι A M s)`.

## Both ends already exist

Nothing about `Proj` or about stalks is reproved here. The two inputs are

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistPowers.nonvanishingLocusDegreeSection`, which computes the
  nonvanishing locus of `degreeSection 𝒜 d a` as `D₊(a)` for any graded ring `𝒜` generated in
  degree one over `𝒜 0` — [Stacks, Tag 01MV] with the invertible locus already dealt with — and
* `SymmetricAlgebra.adjoin_grading_one_eq_top`, which discharges that generation hypothesis for
  `𝒜 = SymmetricAlgebra.grading A M`, since a symmetric algebra is generated by `Sym¹ = M`.

For the pullback the input is `Stacks.NonvanishingPullback.preimage_nonvanishingLocus`,
[Stacks, Tag 0H78] at the scheme spelling: the nonvanishing locus of a pulled-back global section
is the inverse image of the nonvanishing locus. So each result below is a composition.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.pullbackTwistOne`: `f⁎𝒪(1)`, the inverse image along
  `f : Y ⟶ Proj(Sym_A M)` of the first twist.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.pullbackToTwistSections`: `f⁎s`, the inverse image of the
  degree-one global section attached to `s : M`.

## Main results

* `SymmetricAlgebra.nonvanishingLocus_toTwistSections`: **`D₊(s)` is the nonvanishing locus of
  the degree-one section attached to `s`.**
* `Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.preimage_basicOpen_eq_nonvanishingLocus`: **the pullback
  form**, `f⁻¹(D₊(ι A M s)) = Y_{f⁎s}`.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.mem_nonvanishingLocus_pullbackToTwistSections_iff`: the same
  equality pointwise, which is the form a point-by-point argument consumes.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.preimage_basicOpen_eq_top`: **the corollary the global proof
  consumes.** If `f⁎s` is nonvanishing at every point of `Y` then `f` factors through
  `D₊(ι A M s)`.

## Implementation notes

The degree index needs no transport. The twist is indexed by an integer and the section by a
natural number, and `((1 : ℕ) : ℤ)` and `(1 : ℤ)` are definitionally equal, so the statements can
be spelled with the integer literal and `SymmetricAlgebra.toTwistSections`, whose type is
`twistGlobalSections (grading A M) 1`, is accepted directly. The `d * 1` bookkeeping of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistPowers.mem_nonvanishingLocus_degreeSection_iff_of_eq` is
therefore not needed; it is already absorbed into `nonvanishingLocusDegreeSection`.

The hypothesis of `preimage_basicOpen_eq_top` is stated with `Stacks.Ample.nonvanishingLocus`,
the predicate the whole file is about. `Stacks.Ample.mem_nonvanishingLocus_iff` turns it into the
germ condition — the germ of `f⁎s` at `y` is not in `𝔪_y · (f⁎𝒪(1))_y` — which for an invertible
module is exactly that the germ generates the stalk.

The conclusion of `preimage_basicOpen_eq_top` is an equality of opens of `Y`, proved by
`eq_top_iff` and membership rather than by `TopologicalSpace.Opens.ext`: the carrier of `f ⁻¹ᵁ U`
is not syntactically `f.base ⁻¹' U`, so a `change` through the coercion does not fire, while the
membership `y ∈ f ⁻¹ᵁ U` and `f.base y ∈ U` are interchangeable on the nose.

The local reducibility attributes are the ones every file stating `Stacks.Ample.nonvanishingLocus`
at a twisting sheaf carries: without them the module argument, spelled over
`sheafCompose … (structureSheaf 𝒜)`, is not seen as an `(AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜).Modules`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B3V](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B3V)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01MV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01MV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01OB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01OB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0H78](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0H78)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite
open AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj
open RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction

attribute [local implicit_reducible] TopCat.Sheaf sheafCompose
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureSheaf
attribute [local instance_reducible] ProjectiveSpectrum.top

universe u

namespace SymmetricAlgebra

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (M : Type u) [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M]

/-- **`D₊(s)` is the nonvanishing locus of the degree-one section attached to `s`.** For `s : M`
the global section `SymmetricAlgebra.toTwistSections A M s` of `𝒪(1)` on `Proj(Sym_A M)` fails to
vanish exactly on the standard open `D₊(ι A M s)`.

This is [Stacks, Tag 01MV] in the form
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistPowers.nonvanishingLocusDegreeSection`, whose hypothesis of
generation in degree one is `SymmetricAlgebra.adjoin_grading_one_eq_top` for a symmetric
algebra. -/
theorem nonvanishingLocus_toTwistSections (s : M) :
    Stacks.Ample.nonvanishingLocus (X := AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (grading A M))
        (twistingSheaf (grading A M) (1 : ℤ)) (toTwistSections A M s)
      = (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen (grading A M) (ι A M s) :
          Set (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (grading A M))) := by
  rw [← coe_toGradingOne A M s]
  exact Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistPowers.nonvanishingLocusDegreeSection
    (grading A M) (adjoin_grading_one_eq_top A M) 1 (toGradingOne A M s)

end SymmetricAlgebra

namespace Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {M : Type u} [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M]
variable {Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : Y ⟶ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (SymmetricAlgebra.grading A M))

/-- **`f⁎𝒪(1)`**, the inverse image along `f : Y ⟶ Proj(Sym_A M)` of the first twist of the
projective bundle. -/
def pullbackTwistOne : Y.Modules :=
  (modulePullback f.toLRSHom.toShHom).obj
    (twistingSheaf (SymmetricAlgebra.grading A M) (1 : ℤ))

/-- **`f⁎s`**, the inverse image along `f` of the degree-one global section of `𝒪(1)` attached to
`s : M`. It is a global section of `f⁎𝒪(1)`, with no restriction map interposed: the inverse
image of `⊤` is `⊤` on the nose. -/
def pullbackToTwistSections (s : M) : Γ(pullbackTwistOne f, ⊤) :=
  Stacks.NonvanishingPullback.pullbackGlobalSection f
    (twistingSheaf (SymmetricAlgebra.grading A M) (1 : ℤ))
    (SymmetricAlgebra.toTwistSections A M s)

/-- **The pullback form: `f⁻¹(D₊(s)) = Y_{f⁎s}`.** The inverse image of the standard open of
`ι A M s` is the locus on `Y` where the pulled-back degree-one section does not vanish.

`SymmetricAlgebra.nonvanishingLocus_toTwistSections` identifies the standard open with the
nonvanishing locus upstairs, and [Stacks, Tag 0H78]
(`Stacks.NonvanishingPullback.preimage_nonvanishingLocus`) carries that locus down. -/
theorem preimage_basicOpen_eq_nonvanishingLocus (s : M) :
    f.base ⁻¹' (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen (SymmetricAlgebra.grading A M)
        (SymmetricAlgebra.ι A M s) :
          Set (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (SymmetricAlgebra.grading A M)))
      = Stacks.Ample.nonvanishingLocus (pullbackTwistOne f) (pullbackToTwistSections f s) := by
  rw [← SymmetricAlgebra.nonvanishingLocus_toTwistSections A M s]
  exact Stacks.NonvanishingPullback.preimage_nonvanishingLocus f _ _

/-- **The pullback form, pointwise.** A point of `Y` lies in the nonvanishing locus of `f⁎s`
exactly when its image lies in the standard open `D₊(ι A M s)`. -/
theorem mem_nonvanishingLocus_pullbackToTwistSections_iff (s : M) (y : Y) :
    y ∈ Stacks.Ample.nonvanishingLocus (pullbackTwistOne f) (pullbackToTwistSections f s) ↔
      f.base y ∈ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen (SymmetricAlgebra.grading A M)
        (SymmetricAlgebra.ι A M s) :=
  (Set.ext_iff.mp (preimage_basicOpen_eq_nonvanishingLocus f s) y).symm

/-- **If a morphism pulls the degree-one section attached to `s` back to a section that generates
everywhere, then it factors through `D₊(s)`.** This is the local step of clause 3 of
[Stacks, Tag 0B3V]: the hypothesis is instantiated with the section `f⁎s` lifting a generator of
an invertible module, and the conclusion is that `f` lands inside the standard open.

Generation is spelled as membership of `Stacks.Ample.nonvanishingLocus`; by
`Stacks.Ample.mem_nonvanishingLocus_iff` that says the germ of `f⁎s` at `y` is not in
`𝔪_y · (f⁎𝒪(1))_y`, which for an invertible module is exactly that it generates the stalk. -/
theorem preimage_basicOpen_eq_top (s : M)
    (hs : ∀ y : Y, y ∈ Stacks.Ample.nonvanishingLocus (pullbackTwistOne f)
      (pullbackToTwistSections f s)) :
    f ⁻¹ᵁ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen (SymmetricAlgebra.grading A M)
      (SymmetricAlgebra.ι A M s) = ⊤ :=
  eq_top_iff.mpr fun y _ =>
    (mem_nonvanishingLocus_pullbackToTwistSections_iff f s y).mp (hs y)

end Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal

end
